WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.001
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.002
This is "Late Night."

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.437
Hope you're doing well tonight.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.572
And now, if you don't mind,
we are gonna get to the news.

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:09.408
During his speech last night
at a rally

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:11.744
for gubernatorial candidate
Terry McAuliffe,

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:14.079
President Biden attacked
former President Trump

00:00:14.079 --> 00:00:17.082
and said he was "the only
president since Herbert Hoover

00:00:17.082 --> 00:00:20.086
in the '30s to see more jobs
lost than gained."

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.255
Which is why Biden voted
against Trump

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.923
AND Hoover.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:26.092
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.427
During the same speech,
President Biden criticized

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:30.930
Republican candidate
Glenn Youngkin and said

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:35.435
that extremism "can come in
a smile and a fleece vest,"

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:38.171
whereas obstructionism
prefers denim.

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:39.505
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:42.775
That's right, Arizona Senator
Kyrsten Sinema

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:44.944
is receiving attention
on social media

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:47.780
after she wore a denim vest
presiding over the Senate.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.581
Well, she was either
presiding over the Senate

00:00:49.581 --> 00:00:51.251
or the Breakfast Club.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.585
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.587
West Virginia Senator
Joe Manchin complained

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:57.023
during a speech yesterday about
his fellow Senate Democrats

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.858
and said, "I have a hard time

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.861
and I'm totally out of sync
with 48 other Democrats."

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.529
Well, then, just a thought,

00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:05.532
but maybe it's you.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.700
[ Laughter ]
That's like your friend saying

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.537
his last 48 girlfriends
have been psychos.

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:15.708
Like, at that point, it's just,
like, suspicious odds.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.877
According to reports,
a cyclist in Alaska

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:21.214
managed to fight off an attack
from a 500-pound brown bear.

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:22.715
But that was the easy part.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:26.052
The hard part was getting
the bear onto the scale.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:30.389
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:33.225
No, see, this is the worst thing
you can do.

00:01:33.225 --> 00:01:35.561
Because Ian...
So, our writer Ian,

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:38.231
he just sits at home, and what
happens is we send out setups,

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.400
which is, you know,
the first half of the joke.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.235
Ian doesn't do any work.
He doesn't read the news.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:43.970
He doesn't...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.572
All he gets are the setups and
he sees, "Oh, 500-pound bear.

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:48.808
I wonder how they...
you know, a scale?"

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.476
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:52.311
So that's -- you know,
he just -- it's just so --

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:54.581
it's just ba-- it's just --
it's worthless.

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:57.750
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.418
But it filled time.

00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:00.920
It filled time.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.755
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.925
I actually really like
that joke.

00:02:06.925 --> 00:02:09.595
I feel bad now.

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:12.098
Japan's Princess Mako
got married yesterday

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.766
to a so-called commoner,

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.935
which marks the end
of her royal status.

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:19.605
This news first reported by
a very drunk maid of honor.

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:22.442
[Slurring] "I mean,
what were you thinking?"

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.943
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:27.280
"I was there -- Hold on.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.549
I was there when she met him
and I was like,

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.551
[quietly] he's a commoner!"

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.385
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:36.388
A zoo in Colorado announced
this week that 11 lions

00:02:36.388 --> 00:02:39.392
and two tigers have tested
positive for the coronavirus.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:41.727
So far they only have
mild symptoms,

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:43.562
which is more than can be said

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:45.765
for the guy
who had to swab them.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:48.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:51.471
[ Scattered applause ]

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:57.409
I like that eight people
were like,

00:02:57.409 --> 00:02:59.912
[stammering] "Oh, no!

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:02.415
Oh, no, I'm --

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:06.085
I'm clapping for the victim
of a lioncide."

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:09.255
I guess lioncide would maybe be
if you killed a lion.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:12.258
Look it up.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.093
Don't just stare at me,
Shoemaker.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.428
[ Laughs ]

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.096
And finally,
according to a new survey,

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.599
less than 20% of Americans
said that they eat

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:22.434
the wider, yellow end
of candy corn first,

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:26.438
whereas the other 80% actually
turn the candy corn around

00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:28.608
and then chuck it in the trash.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:29.742
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.245
And that was a monologue,
everybody.

